<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 24 February, from 1303 to 1946.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1303">1303 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">723 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Scots defeat an English force at Roslin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a>, a Scottish force led by John Comyn and Sir Simon Fraser ambushed and defeated an English reconnaissance party under Lord John Segrave near the village of Roslin.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1386">1386 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">640 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles III of Naples dies after an attack at Buda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-naples">Charles III of Naples</a>, known as Charles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durazzo</a>, who had seized the Hungarian throne in 1385, died of the wounds he had received in an attack at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a>. He had won <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> by overthrowing his cousin Joanna I.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-naples">Charles III of Naples</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1525">1525 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">501 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Imperial army captures Francis I at the Battle of Pavia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>'s troops routed the French outside Pavia, and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> was taken prisoner. He was released in 1526 only after signing away claims in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pavia">Battle of Pavia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1582">1582 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">444 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Gregory XIII issues the bull reforming the calendar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Inter gravissimas introduced the Gregorian calendar, dropping ten days that October to realign the calendar with the equinox. It is now the world's standard civil calendar.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1803">1803 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">223 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marbury v. Madison establishes judicial review</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chief Justice <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-marshall">John Marshall</a> ruled that the Supreme Court could strike down acts of Congress that conflicted with the Constitution. The decision became a cornerstone of American constitutional law.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1821">1821 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">205 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Plan of Iguala sets out Mexican independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-de-iturbide">Agustín de Iturbide</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicente-guerrero">Vicente Guerrero</a> proclaimed a plan for an independent Mexican monarchy guaranteeing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> and equality. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>'s independence was declared that September.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1920">1920 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler presents the Nazi Party's 25-point programme</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Hofbräuhaus in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>, Hitler read out the programme of the German Workers' Party, which renamed itself the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">National Socialist German Workers' Party</a> (NSDAP) around this time.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1946">1946 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Juan Perón elected President of Argentina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former labour minister won the presidency with strong support from trade unions. With his wife Eva, he built the populist Peronist movement that still shapes Argentine politics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li></ol>
